  "contact_height_control": "Operator was instructed to keep the same contact height and orientation; actual height was not measured or independently confirmed.",
  "interpretation": "Speed 128 closes on the cube in approximately 0.555 s and speed 255 in approximately 0.360 s versus 1.849 s at speed 0. Speed 255 is approximately 5.1 times faster, not ten times faster. The motor stops at 96-99 at speed 255 versus 91-93 at the lower settings. This can reflect dynamic grasp deformation and/or placement variation; these profiles do not separate those causes.",
  "timing_definition": "Time from issuing the close command to the beginning of the final continuous unchanged stopped register/status interval. The extra 0.5 s confirmation interval is excluded. Command communication and register reporting latency are included.",
  "speed255_late_register_changes": "The third cycle first reported a stopped state at approximately 0.355 s with position 98, then reported position 99 at 0.406 s. The first cycle reported status stopped with position 84 before reporting 97 one sample later. Position and status are read sequentially and firmware registers update discretely; these are not synchronized evidence of physical motion after stop.",
  "limitations": [
    "Three cycles per setting are descriptive observations, not a statistical repeatability tolerance.",
    "Motor position is not a loaded TPU fingertip gap or deformation measurement.",
    "Profiles contain no wrist force measurement, so the earlier speed0 resisted-pull target cannot be assumed unchanged at higher closing speed.",
    "No corresponding simulation profile was measured in this analysis; a quantitative sim timing match remains unverified.",
    "The empty speed0 reference is from an earlier same-day recording, not a new interleaved trial."
